            "review_title": "Review at Belly Button",
            "review_text": "Eric Vu\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam189 contributions\n0\nSip, Savor and Chill at Belly Button!\nNov 2025 • Solo\nBelly Button is an impressive new spot for all day activities, from a cup of Cappuccino to a glass of Wine, you name it they've got it. With over hundred bottles displayed, you can browse, choose, and enjoy your wine in a way that feels fun and personal.\n\nOther than that, they offer a unique fusion menu that blends classic brunch favorites with creative Vietnamese touches - everything feels fresh, flavorful, and thoughtfully put together.\nThe food quality is excellent, dishes like Shrimp Tarta Mala, Egg Benedict, or Pana Cotta stand out for their balance and creativity. Portions feel satisfying without being heavy and prices are reasonable for the high-quality offered.\n\nThe atmosphere is another highlight. Located on a quiet street in District 1, the vibes are bright and relaxing, perfect for anything from a casual brunch to a date-night dinner. Whether you sit indoors, at the bar, or on the outdoor terrace, the space feels modern, cozy, and inviting.\n\nOverall, Belly Button delivers great food, standout wines, and a refreshing ambience. Highly recommended if you enjoy brunch culture, good wine, or simply want to experience dining in Saigon.\nRead more\nWritten November 26, 2025",
